{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784202387,"nonce":"4mWsnoNDap2Bud/q2GGCnxe8K/g=","title":"A live acceptance test (Colima/kind, `SCARAB_TEST_KUBE=1`) proving the `clone` mechanism end-to-end on a **public** repo — deliberately not blocked by the token work (S4), so the keystone is validated before the GitHub App adapter lands (ADR-0045 §Mechanism, §Fencing).","message":"A pipeline: `clone` a public repo at a pinned SHA → a downstream `needs:` step reads the checked-out source. Asserts the ADR-0045 invariants observably.\n\n\n- [ ] `clone` of a public repo produces a Pod that checks out the pinned SHA\n- [ ] Working tree **and** `.git` are present in the downstream step's `/workspace` (e.g. `git rev-parse HEAD` == pinned SHA)\n- [ ] `.git/config` in the materialized workspace is credential-free\n- [ ] A downstream `needs: [checkout]` step sees the source files (proves clone→CAS→materialize)\n- [ ] A `depth: full` variant exposes history (`git log` shows \u003e1 commit)\n- [ ] Vanished-SHA case surfaces `SourceUnavailable` fast (no retry loop)\n\n\n- [ADR-0045] clone step kind (c4856cd)\n- [ADR-0045] scarab-clone image (c353bcd)\n- [ADR-0045] CAS materialize/ingest into build_pod (ddead23)","files":null}]}